==Trivia==
*In the upper right corner of the left slide in Legend Stages' [[Cat Base Menu]], there is a hidden Cat face.
*Prior to [[Version 7.1 Update|Version 7.1]], the Legend Stages button in the [[Main Menu]] was labeled Stories of Legend - The Battle Cats.
*Prior to [[Version 10.7 Update|Version 10.7]], Crown difficulties were represented by stars; ★ difficulties below stages did not exist.
*Entering the menu to select Crown difficulties stops stages' splash texts (e.g. Clear up to 1 times!) from flashing.
*Before clearing [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 1, some Legend Stages are already accessible from a menu labeled Event Stage. The menu button will change to say Legend Stages once Chapter 1 is cleared.
*Stories of Legend and Uncanny Legends having 48 sub-chapters each (excluding [[Laboratory of Relics]] and [[Sacred Forest]] respectively, which both contain only one stage) is a reference to the [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapters]], which have 48 stages each.
*Not counting [[Idi:Re]], the first and last new enemies introduced in Stories of Legend are technological variants of the first and last bosses of Empire of Cats. [[Metal Hippoe]] is a cyborg [[Hippoe]], while [[Mecha-Bun (Enemy)|Mecha-Bun]] is a mechanical [[Teacher Bun Bun]].
*Some sub-chapters appear to be named after islands of Japan:
**[[Bamboo Island]] may be a reference to the islets [[wikipedia:Takeshima|Takeshima]], whose name literally means "Bamboo Island".
**[[Sushi Island]]'s Japanese name is quite literally [[wikipedia:Gunkanjima|Gunkanjima]] (軍艦島, "Battleship Island").
**[[Cherry Isles]]' Japanese name, Sakuranbojima (桜んぼ島, "Cherry Island"), is most likely a reference to [[wikipedia:Sakurajima|Sakurajima]] (桜島, "Cherry Blossom Island"), an island-turned-peninsula, an active stratovolcano and the most active volcano in Japan.
**[[Morningstar Isle]]'s Japanese name, Myōjō-oki no Shima (明星おきの島, "Morningstar Island"), is similar to [[wikipedia:Oki Islands|Oki no Shima]] (隠岐の島), a cluster of islands in Shimane Prefecture, Japan. These islands have been inhabited since the Japanese Paleolithic era, connecting them to Uncanny Legends' theme of an ancient past.
**[[Laboratory Island]]'s Japanese name, Rabora Tori-shima (ラボラ・トリ島, "Labora Tori Island"), is a pun on the word ''laboratory'' and possibly ''[[wikipedia:Tori-shima|Tori-shima]]'', an uninhabited volcanic island belonging to the [[wikipedia:Izu Islands|Izu Islands]] of Japan.
*Some aspects of Uncanny Legends may be based on Norse mythology:
**[[Lowkey]] may be named after [[wikipedia:Loki|Loki]].
**[[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs]] (ウルス ''Urusu'') may be named after [[wikipedia:Urðr|Urðr]] (ウルズ ''Uruzu''), while [[wikipedia:Fenrir|Fenrir]] is the name of a monstrous wolf born to Loki and [[wikipedia:Angrboða|Angrboða]].
**[[Rainbow Bridge Toll]] may refer to [[wikipedia:Bifröst|Bifröst]].
**[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Elder Beast Naala]] may represent [[wikipedia:Eikþyrnir|Eikþyrnir]], as Naala is a deer-like creature that is associated with life and appears after [[Silver Current]], which may refer to the rivers created from the water that flows from Eikþyrnir's glowing antlers.
**The [[Media:Bg1028.gif|huge, glowing tree]] in the last 4 Uncanny Legends stages may represent [[wikipedia:Yggdrasil|Yggdrasil]].
**[[Revival of Origin]]'s [[Squire Rel]] or [[Sir Rel]] may represent [[wikipedia:Ratatoskr|Ratatoskr]].
*All 8 Zero Legends sub-chapters from [[The Edge of Spacetime]] take place in a [[Media:Map040.png|jumbled up and mirrored Japan]]. These 8 sub-chapters have a combined total of 48 stages, just like a Main Chapter; the 48th stage, [[Adherence to Virtue]], even has a unique [[Sage of Mind Soractes|boss]] and [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|reward]].
**These 48 stages may specifically represent the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]] of [[Empire of Cats]], which takes place across the 47 prefectures of Japan and [[wikipedia:Iriomote Island|Iriomote Island]] rather than various countries and the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]].
*All Zero Legends sub-chapters from [[Stratospheric Pathway]] through [[Truth's Devouring Maw]] take place in a [[Media:Map042.png|rearranged North and South America]]. This is reflected in both the maps and some of the sub-chapter names:
**[[Konjac Valley]] references the technology hub [[wikipedia:Silicon Valley|Silicon Valley]].
**[[Secluded Cavy Island]]'s Japanese name, Kakusareshi Morumotō (隠されしモルモ島, "Hidden Island of Morumo"), is a possible reference to [[wikipedia:Marmot Island|Marmot Island]], an uninhabited island in the Gulf of Alaska. Morumotō is a pun on ''morumotto'' (モルモット, derived from ''[[wikipedia:Marmot|marmot]]'' but actually refers to a guinea pig, hinting at the sub-chapter's scientific theme) and ''tō'' (島, "island").
**Cruise Ship Panic's Japanese name, Gōka Kyakusen Haipanikku (豪華客船ハイパニック, "Luxury Liner Highpanic"), may be a reference to the sunken ocean liner [[wikipedia:Titanic|RMS ''Titanic'']], as ''Highpanic'' rhymes with ''Titanic''. The ''Titanic''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s wreck lies at the bottom of the Atlantic Ocean 400 nautical miles (740 km) from Newfoundland, Canada, which aligns with how Cruise Ship Panic's map is a rearranged North and South America.
***Cruise Ship Panic may also be based on how North America is the most popular region for [[wikipedia:Cruise ship#Regional industries|cruising]].
*The Zero Legends sub-chapters from [[A Journey of Moments]] through [[Eden of Evolution]] appear to take place in a [[Media:Map048.png|flipped and reversed Eurasia]] with Italy turned into a lake and no Japan or [[wikipedia:Papua (province)|Papua]]. The floating islands on the map may be an homage to [[Floating Continent (Into the Future)|Floating Continent]], since the "final boss" of this part, [[Sage of Selection Darvin]], is an [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]], and the previous map has a [[Immeasurable Power|whirlpool]] resembling [[The Great Abyss (Into the Future)|The Great Abyss]].
**The omission of Japan is likely because The Edge of Spacetime through Garden of Wilted Thoughts already have a Japan-based map.
*The map used in [[New Horizon]] through [[Yandere Chemistry]] appears to be a [[Media:Map053.png|flipped and reversed Australia]], along with some other parts of Oceania and Indonesia.
*[[Unkept Promises]] has the highest energy cost of any main Legend Stage, at 800.
*Many of the stages in [[Here Be Dragons]] through [[Realm of Whyworry]] are harder versions of Stories of Legend stages.
