*All Uncanny Legends stages from [[Shinobi Showdown]] onward contain Relics.
*The early sub-chapters of Zero Legends correspond to different regions of Japan with their stage numbers being influenced by the number of prefectures in the regions. This is shown by the stage locations on the maps as well as dialect being included in stage names.
**[[The Edge of Spacetime]] (6 stages) is for [[wikipedia:Hokkaido|Hokkaido]] (is a single prefecture but also considered to be a region) and the [[wikipedia:Chūgoku region|Chūgoku region]], which has 5 prefectures, making 6 prefectures in total.
**[[Cats Cradle Basin]] (6 stages) is for the [[wikipedia:Tōhoku region|Tōhoku region]], which has 6 prefectures.
**[[The Ururuvu Journals]] (4 stages) is for the [[wikipedia:Shikoku region|Shikoku region]], which has 4 prefectures.
**[[New World Ehen]] (8 stages) is for the [[wikipedia:Kansai region|Kinki region]], which has 7 prefectures and a relatively large island named [[wikipedia:Awaji Island|Awaji Island]].
*Starting from [[Demon of Deciliter Bay]], most Zero Legends sub-chapters contain a stage suited to each of the [[Ultra Form]]s added in the same update. For example, [[Pursuit of Understanding]] is filled with [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] and [[Surge Attack]]s, making it ideal for testing [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Phantasmal Nobunaga]]'s Aku target and Counter-Surge ability.
